568 0 obj
<<
/A 3006 0 R
/Alt (The three-section diagram presents a framework for spatial understanding. The left section, Map environment, displays a grid map with paths connecting yellow pentagon nodes and blue circular nodes. A dashed circular inset highlights a map portion. The middle section, Agent design, features a central robot icon with a clockwise cycle: Observe leads to Decide, Decide leads to Explore, and Explore leads back to Observe. Below the cycle are two lists: Explore methods \(Nearest, Random, Task-based\) and Memory types \(Simple dialogue, Graph-based, Node-sequence, Map-based\). A curved arrow from Map environment points to Observe. A curved arrow from Memory points to the map inset, which then connects to Explore. The right section, Spatial understanding evaluation, lists Reasoning scheme types \(Default thought, Chain-of-thought, Self-consistency, Tree-of-thought\) and Evaluation tasks \(Direction judgement, Distance estimate, Proximity judgement, Density recognition, Path planning\). A straight arrow connects Agent design to Spatial understanding evaluation.)
/K 19
/P 52 0 R
/Pg 15 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
