/A 3015 0 R
/Alt (The map shows a grid background with various light coloured shapes representing background elements. A network of roads, depicted as grey double lines with dashed white centres, traverses the grid. At junctions in the road network are yellow pentagon shapes, which represent road intersections. Connected to these road intersections, often at the end of short road segments, are blue circular shapes, which represent POI nodes. On the right side of the map, explanatory text and two inset examples are presented above a legend. The top text block states, &#x00022;Each POI is linked to its nearest cell, ensuring that POI to POI movement always follow the path.&#x00022; Below this text, the top inset shows a magnified view of a yellow pentagon road intersection connected to a blue circle POI node via a road segment, with a light purple background shape. The next text block states, &#x00022;Road intersections are represented as navigational nodes linking road segments.&#x00022; Below this text, the middle inset shows a magnified view of a yellow pentagon road intersection where three road segments meet. At the bottom right, a legend defines the symbols: a blue circle for &#x00022;POI node&#x00022;, a yellow pentagon for &#x00022;Road intersection&#x00022;, a grey double line with a dashed white centre for &#x00022;Road&#x00022;, and a light grey square for &#x00022;Background&#x00022;.)
