<<
/A 3317 0 R
/Alt (The bar graph displays accuracy percentage on the vertical axis, ranging from minus 5 to 20, for five models on the horizontal axis: GPT, Gemini, Claude, Qwen, and DeepSeek. Three data series are presented: CoT-DT, SC-CoT-DT, and ToT-DT. For GPT, CoT-DT shows a negative accuracy gain, SC-CoT-DT shows a small positive gain, and ToT-DT shows a positive gain, which is the highest among the three for GPT. For Gemini, CoT-DT shows a negative gain, SC-CoT-DT shows a gain near zero, and ToT-DT shows a negative gain, which is the lowest among the three for Gemini. For Claude, all methods show positive gains, with ToT-DT being the highest, followed by SC-CoT-DT, then CoT-DT. For Qwen, all methods show positive gains, with SC-CoT-DT being the highest, followed by ToT-DT, then CoT-DT. For DeepSeek, all methods show positive gains, with ToT-DT being significantly higher than the other two, followed by SC-CoT-DT, then CoT-DT. Overall, ToT-DT generally achieves the highest accuracy gains across models, notably for Claude and DeepSeek. SC-CoT-DT often shows the second highest gains. GPT and Gemini models exhibit mixed results, including negative accuracy gains for some methods, while Claude, Qwen, and DeepSeek consistently show positive accuracy gains across all methods, with DeepSeek showing the largest overall gains.)
/K 7
/P 52 0 R
/Pg 32 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
